# API Design Review

## REST Checklist

- Resource names: nouns, plural, lowercase hyphenated (`/shipping-addresses`).
- HTTP methods correct: GET side-effect free, POST creates/triggers, PUT replaces, PATCH updates, DELETE removes.
- Status codes correct: 201+Location for created, 204 for delete, 400/401/403/404/409/422/429/500.
- All list endpoints paginated — no unbounded responses.
- Error responses have consistent shape across all endpoints (code, message, field errors).
- No stack traces or internal paths in error responses.
- API version explicit (URI or header). Breaking changes only in new version.
- Deprecation communicated via `Deprecation`/`Sunset` headers.

## Breaking Change Detection

Breaking: removing/renaming fields, adding required request fields, changing types.
Non-breaking: new optional fields, new endpoints.

## GraphQL Checklist

- List fields have pagination args. Mutations return mutated object.
- Resolvers protected against N+1 (DataLoader/batching).
- Schema changes follow `@deprecated` before removal.

## Output Format

```markdown
## API Design Findings

**[P1]** `path/file.ext:line` - Title
Issue and fix direction.

## Summary
Consistency verdict and most impactful issues.
```
